@* BrandHeader — chrome content rendered inside MudAppBar by MainLayout.
 *
 * Spec authority: docs/ui/screens/answer-with-citations.md § Screen zones
 * #1 ("Brand mark on the left, 'What we cover' link on the right").
 * The chrome is intentionally minimal — one outbound link that surfaces
 * the coverage-transparency posture immediately.
 *
 * Rationale (per docs/PHASE5-DRIFT-AUDIT.md § 3): a 4-link nav reads as a
 * generic SaaS site. "Home" is internally redundant with the brand mark
 * (brand → /). "Wizard" is the same destination as / once landing renders
 * the Wizard surface (ADR-0026 § 1: / = landing, /wizard = primary surface).
 * "Status" belongs in the footer per ADR-0027 § 1 (no captive-UI status
 * surfaces in the prospect-facing chrome).
 *
 * Logo: text-only placeholder. SVG/PNG asset arrives as a follow-up.
 * The read-only admin showcase is surfaced here ('Behind the Scenes' → /admin);
 * mutations there are gated to signed-in admins.
 *
 * ADR-0008 — MudBlazor strict (uses MudLink + MudButton + MudSpacer)
 * ADR-0026 § 1 — routing inventory
 * ADR-0027 § 1 — community-resource posture (no captive UI)
 *@

<MudLink Href="/"
         Class="brand-logo ml-2 mr-4"
         Typo="Typo.h6"
         Color="Color.Inherit"
         Underline="Underline.None"
         aria-label="PinballWizard home">
    &#x25CF; PinballWizard
</MudLink>

<MudSpacer />

<nav aria-label="Main navigation">
    <MudButton Href="/about"
               Variant="Variant.Text"
               Color="Color.Inherit"
               Class="nav-link"
               aria-label="What we cover">
        What we cover
    </MudButton>
    <MudButton Href="/admin"
               Variant="Variant.Text"
               Color="Color.Inherit"
               Class="nav-link"
               aria-label="Behind the Scenes — admin showcase">
        Behind the Scenes
    </MudButton>
</nav>
